{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HT6fRpvoVLe9BPjNLuWhnP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport { ApiTable } from \"@/components/api-table.tsx\";\n2\timport {\n3\t  CustomizingYourThemeColors,\n4\t  ResponsiveDesign,\n5\t  TargetingSpecificStates,\n6\t  UsingACustomValue,\n7\t} from \"@/components/content.tsx\";\n8\timport { Example } from \"@/components/example.tsx\";\n9\timport { Figure } from \"@/components/figure.tsx\";\n10\timport colors from \"./utils/colors\";\n11\timport dedent from \"dedent\";\n12\t\n13\texport const title = \"border-color\";\n14\texport const description = \"Utilities for controlling the color of an element's borders.\";\n15\t\n16\t<ApiTable\n17\t  rows={[\n18\t    ...[\n19\t      [\"border\", (value) => `border-color: ${value}`],\n20\t      [\"border-x\", (value) => `border-inline-color: ${value}`],\n21\t      [\"border-y\", (value) => `border-block-color: ${value}`],\n22\t      [\"border-s\", (value) => `border-inline-start-color: ${value}`],\n23\t      [\"border-e\", (value) => `border-inline-end-color: ${value}`],\n24\t      [\"border-bs\", (value) => `border-block-start-color: ${value}`],\n25\t      [\"border-be\", (value) => `border-block-end-color: ${value}`],\n26\t      [\"border-t\", (value) => `border-top-color: ${value}`],\n27\t      [\"border-r\", (value) => `border-right-color: ${value}`],\n28\t      [\"border-b\", (value) => `border-bottom-color: ${value}`],\n29\t      [\"border-l\", (value) => `border-left-color: ${value}`],\n30\t      [\"divide\", (value) => `& > :not(:last-child) {\\n  border-color: ${value}\\n}`],\n31\t    ].flatMap(([utility, css]) => [\n32\t      [`${utility}-inherit`, css(\"inherit;\")],\n33\t      [`${utility}-current`, css(\"currentColor;\")],\n34\t      [`${utility}-transparent`, css(\"transparent;\")],\n35\t      ...Object.entries(colors).map(([name, value]) => [\n36\t        `${utility}-${name}`,\n37\t        css(`var(--color-${name}); /* ${value} */`),\n38\t      ]),\n39\t      [`${utility}-(<custom-property>)`, css(\"var(<custom-property>);\")],\n40\t      [`${utility}-[<value>]`, css(\"<value>;\")],\n41\t    ]),\n42\t  ]}\n43\t/>\n44\t\n45\t## Examples\n46\t\n47\t### Basic example\n48\t\n49\tUse utilities like `border-rose-500` and `border-lime-100` to control the border color of an element:\n50\t\n51\t<Figure>\n52\t\n53\t<Example>\n54\t  {\n55\t    <div className=\"grid gap-4 text-center text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-white lg:grid-cols-3\">\n56\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n57\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n58\t          border-indigo-500\n59\t        </p>\n60\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n61\t      </div>\n62\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n63\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n64\t          border-purple-500\n65\t        </p>\n66\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-purple-500 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n67\t      </div>\n68\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n69\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n70\t          border-sky-500\n71\t        </p>\n72\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-sky-500 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n73\t      </div>\n74\t    </div>\n75\t  }\n76\t</Example>\n77\t\n78\t```html\n79\t<!-- [!code classes:border-indigo-500,border-purple-500,border-sky-500] -->\n80\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n81\t<div class=\"border-4 border-purple-500 ...\"></div>\n82\t<div class=\"border-4 border-sky-500 ...\"></div>\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\t</Figure>\n86\t\n87\t### Changing the opacity\n88\t\n89\tUse the color opacity modifier to control the opacity of an element's border color:\n90\t\n91\t<Figure>\n92\t\n93\t<Example>\n94\t  {\n95\t    <div className=\"grid gap-4 text-center text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-white lg:grid-cols-3\">\n96\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n97\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n98\t          border-indigo-500/100\n99\t        </p>\n100\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-500/100 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n101\t      </div>\n102\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n103\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n104\t          border-indigo-500/75\n105\t        </p>\n106\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-500/75 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n107\t      </div>\n108\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n109\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n110\t          border-indigo-500/50\n111\t        </p>\n112\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-500/50 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n113\t      </div>\n114\t    </div>\n115\t  }\n116\t</Example>\n117\t\n118\t```html\n119\t<!-- [!code word:/100] -->\n120\t<!-- [!code word:/75] -->\n121\t<!-- [!code word:/50] -->\n122\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-500/100 ...\"></div>\n123\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-500/75 ...\"></div>\n124\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-500/50 ...\"></div>\n125\t```\n126\t\n127\t</Figure>\n128\t\n129\t### Individual sides\n130\t\n131\tUse utilities like `border-t-indigo-500` and `border-r-lime-100` to set the border color for one side of an element:\n132\t\n133\t<Figure>\n134\t\n135\t<Example>\n136\t  {\n137\t    <div className=\"grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-4 gap-y-8 text-center text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-white sm:grid-cols-2\">\n138\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n139\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n140\t          border-t-indigo-500\n141\t        </p>\n142\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-t-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-t-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n143\t      </div>\n144\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n145\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n146\t          border-r-indigo-500\n147\t        </p>\n148\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-r-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-r-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n149\t      </div>\n150\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n151\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n152\t          border-b-indigo-500\n153\t        </p>\n154\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-b-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-b-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n155\t      </div>\n156\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n157\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n158\t          border-l-indigo-500\n159\t        </p>\n160\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-l-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-l-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n161\t      </div>\n162\t    </div>\n163\t  }\n164\t</Example>\n165\t\n166\t```html\n167\t<!-- [!code classes:border-t-indigo-500,border-r-indigo-500,border-b-indigo-500,border-l-indigo-500] -->\n168\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-t-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n169\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-r-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n170\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-b-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n171\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-l-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n172\t```\n173\t\n174\t</Figure>\n175\t\n176\t### Horizontal and vertical sides\n177\t\n178\tUse utilities like `border-x-indigo-500` and `border-y-lime-100` to set the border color on two sides of an element at the same time:\n179\t\n180\t<Figure>\n181\t\n182\t<Example>\n183\t  {\n184\t    <div className=\"flex flex-col items-center justify-around gap-4 text-center text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-white sm:flex-row\">\n185\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n186\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n187\t          border-x-indigo-500\n188\t        </p>\n189\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-x-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-x-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n190\t      </div>\n191\t      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n192\t        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n193\t          border-y-indigo-500\n194\t        </p>\n195\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-y-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-y-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n196\t      </div>\n197\t    </div>\n198\t  }\n199\t</Example>\n200\t\n201\t```html\n202\t<!-- [!code classes:border-x-indigo-500,border-y-indigo-500] -->\n203\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-x-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n204\t<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-y-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\t</Figure>\n208\t\n209\t### Using logical properties\n210\t\n211\tUse utilities like `border-s-indigo-500` and `border-e-lime-100` to set the `border-inline-start-color` and `border-inline-end-color` [logical properties](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_Logical_Properties/Basic_concepts), which map to either the left or right border based on the text direction:\n212\t\n213\t<Figure>\n214\t\n215\t<Example>\n216\t  {\n217\t    <div className=\"grid grid-cols-2 place-items-center gap-x-4\">\n218\t      <div className=\"flex flex-col items-start gap-y-4\" dir=\"ltr\">\n219\t        <p className=\"text-sm font-medium\">Left-to-right</p>\n220\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-s-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-s-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n221\t      </div>\n222\t      <div className=\"flex flex-col items-start gap-y-4\" dir=\"rtl\">\n223\t        <p className=\"text-sm font-medium\">Right-to-left</p>\n224\t        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-s-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-s-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n225\t      </div>\n226\t    </div>\n227\t  }\n228\t</Example>\n229\t\n230\t```html\n231\t<!-- [!code classes:border-s-indigo-500,border-s-indigo-500] -->\n232\t<!-- [!code word:dir=\"ltr\"] -->\n233\t<!-- [!code word:dir=\"rtl\"] -->\n234\t<div dir=\"ltr\">\n235\t  <div class=\"border-s-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n236\t</div>\n237\t<div dir=\"rtl\">\n238\t  <div class=\"border-s-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n239\t</div>\n240\t```\n241\t\n242\t</Figure>\n243\t\n244\tUse the `border-bs-*` and `border-be-*` utilities to set the `border-block-start-color` and `border-block-end-color` logical properties, which map to either the top or bottom border based on the writing mode:\n245\t\n246\t```html\n247\t<!-- [!code classes:border-bs-indigo-500] -->\n248\t<div class=\"border-bs-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n249\t```\n250\t\n251\t### Divider between children\n252\t\n253\tUse utilities like `divide-indigo-500` and `divide-lime-100` to control the border color between child elements:\n254\t\n255\t<Figure>\n256\t\n257\t<Example>\n258\t  {\n259\t    <div className=\"mx-auto grid max-w-lg grid-cols-3 divide-x-4 divide-indigo-500 rounded-lg text-center font-mono text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-gray-400\">\n260\t      <div className=\"p-4 outline-1 -outline-offset-1 outline-gray-900/20 outline-dashed dark:outline-white/20\">01</div>\n261\t      <div className=\"p-4 outline-1 -outline-offset-1 outline-gray-900/20 outline-dashed dark:outline-white/20\">02</div>\n262\t      <div className=\"p-4 outline-1 -outline-offset-1 outline-gray-900/20 outline-dashed dark:outline-white/20\">03</div>\n263\t    </div>\n264\t  }\n265\t</Example>\n266\t\n267\t```html\n268\t<!-- [!code classes:divide-indigo-500] -->\n269\t<div class=\"grid grid-cols-3 divide-x-4 divide-indigo-500\">\n270\t  <div>01</div>\n271\t  <div>02</div>\n272\t  <div>03</div>\n273\t</div>\n274\t```\n275\t\n276\t</Figure>\n277\t\n278\t### Using a custom value\n279\t\n280\t<UsingACustomValue utility=\"border\" name=\"border color\" value=\"#243c5a\" />\n281\t\n282\t### Applying on focus\n283\t\n284\t<TargetingSpecificStates property=\"border-color\" variant=\"focus\">\n285\t\n286\t<Figure>\n287\t\n288\t<Example>\n289\t  {\n290\t    <label className=\"mx-auto block max-w-xs\">\n291\t      <span className=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-200\">Email address</span>\n292\t      <input\n293\t        type=\"text\"\n294\t        placeholder=\"jane@example.com\"\n295\t        className=\"block w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-gray-700 px-3 py-2 font-sans text-sm leading-5 text-gray-500 focus:border-pink-600 focus:outline-none dark:bg-gray-900 dark:text-gray-400 dark:placeholder:text-gray-600\"\n296\t      />\n297\t    </label>\n298\t  }\n299\t</Example>\n300\t\n301\t```html\n302\t<!-- [!code classes:focus:border-pink-600] -->\n303\t<input class=\"border-2 border-gray-700 focus:border-pink-600 ...\" />\n304\t```\n305\t\n306\t</Figure>\n307\t\n308\t</TargetingSpecificStates>\n309\t\n310\t### Responsive design\n311\t\n312\t<ResponsiveDesign property=\"border-color\" defaultClass=\"border-blue-500\" featuredClass=\"border-green-500\" />\n313\t\n314\t## Customizing your theme\n315\t\n316\t<CustomizingYourThemeColors utility=\"border\" />\n317\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ff1018a-54db-4e05-afc0-426a0ce9c3ad","uuid":"735c3fc7-bdd4-4738-abe8-5982b20320a8","timestamp":"2026-09-24T21:22:02.695Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jcarr/.cache/markdownattractor/bench/tailwindcss/src/docs/border-color.mdx","content":"import { ApiTable } from \"@/components/api-table.tsx\";\nimport {\n  CustomizingYourThemeColors,\n  ResponsiveDesign,\n  TargetingSpecificStates,\n  UsingACustomValue,\n} from \"@/components/content.tsx\";\nimport { Example } from \"@/components/example.tsx\";\nimport { Figure } from \"@/components/figure.tsx\";\nimport colors from \"./utils/colors\";\nimport dedent from \"dedent\";\n\nexport const title = \"border-color\";\nexport const description = \"Utilities for controlling the color of an element's borders.\";\n\n<ApiTable\n  rows={[\n    ...[\n      [\"border\", (value) => `border-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-x\", (value) => `border-inline-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-y\", (value) => `border-block-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-s\", (value) => `border-inline-start-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-e\", (value) => `border-inline-end-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-bs\", (value) => `border-block-start-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-be\", (value) => `border-block-end-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-t\", (value) => `border-top-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-r\", (value) => `border-right-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-b\", (value) => `border-bottom-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"border-l\", (value) => `border-left-color: ${value}`],\n      [\"divide\", (value) => `& > :not(:last-child) {\\n  border-color: ${value}\\n}`],\n    ].flatMap(([utility, css]) => [\n      [`${utility}-inherit`, css(\"inherit;\")],\n      [`${utility}-current`, css(\"currentColor;\")],\n      [`${utility}-transparent`, css(\"transparent;\")],\n      ...Object.entries(colors).map(([name, value]) => [\n        `${utility}-${name}`,\n        css(`var(--color-${name}); /* ${value} */`),\n      ]),\n      [`${utility}-(<custom-property>)`, css(\"var(<custom-property>);\")],\n      [`${utility}-[<value>]`, css(\"<value>;\")],\n    ]),\n  ]}\n/>\n\n## Examples\n\n### Basic example\n\nUse utilities like `border-rose-500` and `border-lime-100` to control the border color of an element:\n\n<Figure>\n\n<Example>\n  {\n    <div className=\"grid gap-4 text-center text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-white lg:grid-cols-3\">\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-indigo-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-purple-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-purple-500 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-sky-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-sky-500 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  }\n</Example>\n\n```html\n<!-- [!code classes:border-indigo-500,border-purple-500,border-sky-500] -->\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n<div class=\"border-4 border-purple-500 ...\"></div>\n<div class=\"border-4 border-sky-500 ...\"></div>\n```\n\n</Figure>\n\n### Changing the opacity\n\nUse the color opacity modifier to control the opacity of an element's border color:\n\n<Figure>\n\n<Example>\n  {\n    <div className=\"grid gap-4 text-center text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-white lg:grid-cols-3\">\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-indigo-500/100\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-500/100 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-indigo-500/75\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-500/75 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-indigo-500/50\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-500/50 bg-white p-4 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  }\n</Example>\n\n```html\n<!-- [!code word:/100] -->\n<!-- [!code word:/75] -->\n<!-- [!code word:/50] -->\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-500/100 ...\"></div>\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-500/75 ...\"></div>\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-500/50 ...\"></div>\n```\n\n</Figure>\n\n### Individual sides\n\nUse utilities like `border-t-indigo-500` and `border-r-lime-100` to set the border color for one side of an element:\n\n<Figure>\n\n<Example>\n  {\n    <div className=\"grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-4 gap-y-8 text-center text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-white sm:grid-cols-2\">\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-t-indigo-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-t-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-t-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-r-indigo-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-r-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-r-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-b-indigo-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-b-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-b-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-l-indigo-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-l-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-l-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  }\n</Example>\n\n```html\n<!-- [!code classes:border-t-indigo-500,border-r-indigo-500,border-b-indigo-500,border-l-indigo-500] -->\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-t-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-r-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-b-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-l-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n```\n\n</Figure>\n\n### Horizontal and vertical sides\n\nUse utilities like `border-x-indigo-500` and `border-y-lime-100` to set the border color on two sides of an element at the same time:\n\n<Figure>\n\n<Example>\n  {\n    <div className=\"flex flex-col items-center justify-around gap-4 text-center text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-white sm:flex-row\">\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-x-indigo-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-x-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-x-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col items-center\">\n        <p className=\"mb-3 text-center font-mono text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400\">\n          border-y-indigo-500\n        </p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-y-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-y-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  }\n</Example>\n\n```html\n<!-- [!code classes:border-x-indigo-500,border-y-indigo-500] -->\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-x-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n<div class=\"border-4 border-indigo-200 border-y-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n```\n\n</Figure>\n\n### Using logical properties\n\nUse utilities like `border-s-indigo-500` and `border-e-lime-100` to set the `border-inline-start-color` and `border-inline-end-color` [logical properties](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_Logical_Properties/Basic_concepts), which map to either the left or right border based on the text direction:\n\n<Figure>\n\n<Example>\n  {\n    <div className=\"grid grid-cols-2 place-items-center gap-x-4\">\n      <div className=\"flex flex-col items-start gap-y-4\" dir=\"ltr\">\n        <p className=\"text-sm font-medium\">Left-to-right</p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-s-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-s-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"flex flex-col items-start gap-y-4\" dir=\"rtl\">\n        <p className=\"text-sm font-medium\">Right-to-left</p>\n        <div className=\"size-16 border-4 border-indigo-200 border-s-indigo-500 bg-white p-4 ring-1 ring-gray-900/5 dark:border-indigo-600/20 dark:border-s-indigo-500 dark:bg-gray-900\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  }\n</Example>\n\n```html\n<!-- [!code classes:border-s-indigo-500,border-s-indigo-500] -->\n<!-- [!code word:dir=\"ltr\"] -->\n<!-- [!code word:dir=\"rtl\"] -->\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\n  <div class=\"border-s-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n</div>\n<div dir=\"rtl\">\n  <div class=\"border-s-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n</div>\n```\n\n</Figure>\n\nUse the `border-bs-*` and `border-be-*` utilities to set the `border-block-start-color` and `border-block-end-color` logical properties, which map to either the top or bottom border based on the writing mode:\n\n```html\n<!-- [!code classes:border-bs-indigo-500] -->\n<div class=\"border-bs-indigo-500 ...\"></div>\n```\n\n### Divider between children\n\nUse utilities like `divide-indigo-500` and `divide-lime-100` to control the border color between child elements:\n\n<Figure>\n\n<Example>\n  {\n    <div className=\"mx-auto grid max-w-lg grid-cols-3 divide-x-4 divide-indigo-500 rounded-lg text-center font-mono text-sm leading-6 font-bold text-gray-400\">\n      <div className=\"p-4 outline-1 -outline-offset-1 outline-gray-900/20 outline-dashed dark:outline-white/20\">01</div>\n      <div className=\"p-4 outline-1 -outline-offset-1 outline-gray-900/20 outline-dashed dark:outline-white/20\">02</div>\n      <div className=\"p-4 outline-1 -outline-offset-1 outline-gray-900/20 outline-dashed dark:outline-white/20\">03</div>\n    </div>\n  }\n</Example>\n\n```html\n<!-- [!code classes:divide-indigo-500] -->\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-3 divide-x-4 divide-indigo-500\">\n  <div>01</div>\n  <div>02</div>\n  <div>03</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n</Figure>\n\n### Using a custom value\n\n<UsingACustomValue utility=\"border\" name=\"border color\" value=\"#243c5a\" />\n\n### Applying on focus\n\n<TargetingSpecificStates property=\"border-color\" variant=\"focus\">\n\n<Figure>\n\n<Example>\n  {\n    <label className=\"mx-auto block max-w-xs\">\n      <span className=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-200\">Email address</span>\n      <input\n        type=\"text\"\n        placeholder=\"jane@example.com\"\n        className=\"block w-full rounded-lg border-2 border-gray-700 px-3 py-2 font-sans text-sm leading-5 text-gray-500 focus:border-pink-600 focus:outline-none dark:bg-gray-900 dark:text-gray-400 dark:placeholder:text-gray-600\"\n      />\n    </label>\n  }\n</Example>\n\n```html\n<!-- [!code classes:focus:border-pink-600] -->\n<input class=\"border-2 border-gray-700 focus:border-pink-600 ...\" />\n```\n\n</Figure>\n\n</TargetingSpecificStates>\n\n### Responsive design\n\n<ResponsiveDesign property=\"border-color\" defaultClass=\"border-blue-500\" featuredClass=\"border-green-500\" />\n\n## Customizing your theme\n\n<CustomizingYourThemeColors utility=\"border\" />\n","numLines":317,"startLine":1,"totalLines":317}}}
